title: JadePuffer Agentic Ransomware Cron Beacon to Fixed C2 Endpoint
id: 51d8f00c-2dca-4dcc-90b3-766e9a5193b8
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects network connections to 45.131.66.106 TCP/4444, the fixed
    command-and-control endpoint of the JadePuffer agentic ransomware
    operation (Sysdig, 2026): the intruder persisted with a cron job
    beaconing to this endpoint every 30 minutes after exploiting Langflow
    CVE-2025-3248, then encrypted 1,342 Alibaba Nacos configuration items.
references:
    - https://www.sysdig.com/blog/jadepuffer-agentic-ransomware-for-automated-database-extortion
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/jadepuffer-ransomware-used-ai-agent-to-automate-entire-attack/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/29
tags:
    - attack.t1053
logsource:
    category: network_connection
detection:
    selection:
        DestinationIp: 45.131.66.106
        DestinationPort: 4444
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Unlikely; any connection to this fixed attacker endpoint should be
      investigated, but re-check for spoofed or redirected telemetry first
level: high
